00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:09,000
Planet 51 is a 2009 Spanish-British-American animated science fiction comedy
film directed by Jorge Blanco from a script by Joe Stillman.

12
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
Starring the voices of Dwayne Johnson, Justin Long, Jessica Biel, Gary Oldman, Seann William Scott, John Cleese and Freddie Benedict, the film
follows an astronaut who lands on an alien planet, as one of the aliens helps him return to his ship while evading the military.

13
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:15,000
An international co-production between Spain, the United Kingdom, and the United States, the film was originally
acquired for North American distribution by New Line Cinema, but then sold to Sony Pictures before completion.

14
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:48,000
Originally titled Planet One, and later named as an allusion to Area 51, the film was completed on a $70
million budget, which, at the time of its release, was the most expensive film produced in Spain.

15
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
Planet 51 was released on 20 November 2009, in the United States and Canada by Sony Pictures Releasing's TriStar Pictures and Remstar Media Partners
respectively, on 27 November in Spain by DeAPlaneta Distribución, and 4 December in the United Kingdom by HandMade Films International.

16
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
The film grossed $105.6 million in the worldwide box office.

17
01:17:21,000 --> 01:17:27,000
While the film was well received in Spain, earning a Goya Award for Best Animated
Film, it received generally negative reviews from American critics.

18
01:21:54,000 --> 01:22:00,000
The film explores themes of spacecraft, flying saucer,
alien life-form, alien, alien planet.

19
01:26:27,000 --> 01:26:33,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
